    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.trailspace\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI can't figure out how to get it to stop in buffers that I don't care about.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'WinEnter', 'BufEnter', 'InsertLeave' }, {\r\n  desc = \"Stop highlighting trailing white space\",\r\n  group = group,\r\n  callback = function(ev)\r\n    -- If we ask for trailing whitespace, respect it\r\n    if string.find(vim.bo[ev.buf].formatoptions, \"w\") ~= nil then\r\n      MiniTrailspace.unhighlight()\r\n    end\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm thinking this is related to order of operations and the mini.trailspace autocommands might be running first.",
